    "numeric": "equal to the CPU reference bloom::render::convertNativeSamples for every layout: additions, subtractions and multiplications are precise (no contraction), divisions are an integer long division with round-to-nearest-even, binary16 is decoded from its bits; only the legacy inverse transfer curves (transfer 1, 6, 13) use pow() and are held to 2e-6 absolute or relative per finite component",
    "alpha": "zero alpha publishes transparent black exactly as Rgba32f::fromPremultiplied; stored samples encode alpha as a * 0.5 + 0.5, which equals fma(a, 0.5, 0.5)",
    "ingestPolicy": "binary16 NaN/Inf become zero and alpha is clamped to [0, 1], the OpenEXR decoder's policy",
